{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "model": "SidecarHistory",
  "assumptions": [
    "The source supplies immutable complete before and after values before retiring live chunks.",
    "One source transaction has monotonically numbered operations and at most one rollback to the savepoint before RollbackAt.",
    "WAL append and one-record-prefix flush are separate atomic actions; crash discards only the volatile suffix.",
    "A fragment record is written atomically; torn records and checksum collisions are outside this model.",
    "Every registered consumer starts at the beginning and keeps its durable cursor; consumer membership is fixed.",
    "The historical enumerator has an independent stable scan cursor and logical event sequence; its crash and network delivery failures are outside source/replica process crash budgets.",
    "Source recovery scans retained WAL before archive deletion resumes, aborting an uncommitted source transaction.",
    "The source retains the entire transaction dependency interval until every registered consumer passes its events.",
    "Replica local commit atomically persists all uncancelled operations of one source transaction and its progress; per-operation fragments and the assembled transaction batch remain volatile until that commit.",
    "Crashes have explicit finite admission budgets; durable storage, decoding, recovery, and registered consumers are weakly fair and remain available afterward."
  ],
